1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,034
A plane on autopilot climbs

2
00:00:02,034 --> 00:00:03,240
over a mountain.

3
00:00:03,240 --> 00:00:04,747
Who gets the credit,

4
00:00:04,747 --> 00:00:06,707
the mountain or the plane?

5
00:00:06,707 --> 00:00:08,471
The plane has radar and

6
00:00:08,471 --> 00:00:10,542
a control system that sense

7
00:00:10,542 --> 00:00:12,384
the terrain and respond.

8
00:00:12,384 --> 00:00:14,532
Dr. Randy Guliuzza uses this

9
00:00:14,532 --> 00:00:16,296
picture to make a point

10
00:00:16,296 --> 00:00:17,830
about living things.

11
00:00:17,830 --> 00:00:20,342
He argues organisms are engineered

12
00:00:20,342 --> 00:00:22,779
with internal systems that detect

13
00:00:22,779 --> 00:00:25,217
conditions and adjust on purpose.

14
00:00:25,217 --> 00:00:27,655
The environment is something they

15
00:00:27,655 --> 00:00:29,280
read, not a force that

16
00:00:29,280 --> 00:00:30,831
molds them like clay.

17
00:00:30,831 --> 00:00:33,388
He calls this engineering thinking:

18
00:00:33,388 --> 00:00:36,091
explain biology with measurable parts

19
00:00:36,091 --> 00:00:37,406
and whole systems,

20
00:00:37,406 --> 00:00:39,159
and look for the sensors

21
00:00:39,159 --> 00:00:41,570
and controls inside the organism.

22
00:00:41,570 --> 00:00:42,721
If that's right,

23
00:00:42,721 --> 00:00:45,024
Yahweh built creatures to handle

24
00:00:45,024 --> 00:00:46,751
the world He placed them

25
00:00:46,751 --> 00:00:48,118
in. Next: a new way

26
00:00:48,118 --> 00:00:48,981
to see life.
